\section{Verification Operators and Invariant Audits}

Let $\mathcal{I}_{\text{TSSE}}$ denote the set of TSSE invariants:
\[
\mathcal{I}_{\text{TSSE}} =
\left\{
\mathcal{I}_{\text{T}},\;
\mathcal{I}_{\text{R}},\;
\mathcal{I}_{\text{F}}
\right\}.
\]

Define the verification operator:
\[
\mathcal{V}_{\mathcal{I}} : (q,p) \mapsto \mathcal{I}_{\text{TSSE}}(q,p),
\]
which evaluates invariants at any point in phase-space.

\begin{definition}[TSSE Verification Operator]
A verification operator $\mathcal{V}_{\mathcal{I}}$ satisfies:
\[
\mathcal{V}_{\mathcal{I}}(\mathcal{U}(t)(q,p)) = \mathcal{V}_{\mathcal{I}}(q,p).
\]
\end{definition}

\begin{lemma}[Verification Operator Commutation]
Verification operators commute with TSSE evolution:
\[
\mathcal{V}_{\mathcal{I}}\mathcal{U}(t) = \mathcal{U}(t)\mathcal{V}_{\mathcal{I}}.
\]
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Since invariants are preserved under TSSE evolution, applying $\mathcal{V}_{\mathcal{I}}$
before or after $\mathcal{U}(t)$ yields identical results.
\end{proof}

This lemma establishes the algebraic consistency of invariant verification.

