\section{Manifold Integrity Tests Under Extreme Loads}

Let $\mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE–AITFE}}$ denote the composite structural manifold.

Define the manifold deviation metric:
\[
\delta_{\mathcal{S}}(t) =
\text{dist}\left(
\mathcal{U}_{\epsilon}(t)(q,p),\;
\mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE–AITFE}}
\right).
\]

\begin{lemma}[Manifold Stability Under Perturbation]
If $\Delta H$ preserves manifold closure, then:
\[
\delta_{\mathcal{S}}(t) = 0.
\]
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Manifold closure ensures that all trajectories remain within
$\mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE–AITFE}}$.
\end{proof}

\begin{theorem}[Manifold Robustness]
If $\Delta H$ is TSSE-admissible, then:
\[
\delta_{\mathcal{S}}(t) = \mathcal{O}(\epsilon).
\]
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Manifold deviation scales linearly with perturbation magnitude for admissible
perturbations.
\end{proof}

This theorem ensures structural stability of TSSE engines under extreme loads.

