\section{Canonical TSSE Verification Kernel (TSSE-VK)}

Define the TSSE Verification Kernel:
\[
\mathcal{K}_{\text{TSSE-VK}} =
\left(
\mathcal{V}_{\mathcal{I}},\;
H_{\epsilon},\;
\mathcal{S}_{\text{TSSE–AITFE}},\;
\delta_{\mathcal{T}},\;
\delta_{\mathcal{S}},\;
\mathcal{U}_{\epsilon}(t)
\right).
\]

It enforces:
\[
\mathcal{V}_{\mathcal{I}}(\mathcal{U}_{\epsilon}(t)(q,p))
=
\mathcal{V}_{\mathcal{I}}(q,p),
\]
\[
\delta_{\mathcal{T}}(t) = \mathcal{O}(\epsilon),
\qquad
\delta_{\mathcal{S}}(t) = \mathcal{O}(\epsilon),
\]
\[
\mathcal{U}_{\epsilon}(t)^\top J\,\mathcal{U}_{\epsilon}(t) = J.
\]

This kernel defines the complete TSSE verification and stress-test architecture.

